			(property "Description" "TE Connectivity 63951-1 FASTON PC board tab (male blade), RIGHT-ANGLE style -- .250in (6.35mm +/-0.08) wide x .033-.030in (0.83-0.77mm) thick, brass with tin over nickel plate, App Spec 114-2115 (same governing spec as the straight TE_63849-1 and the owner-referenced .187-series 1217061-1). Geometry per TE's own customer drawing C=63951 rev L2 (lib/datasheets/TE_63951-1.pdf): a FLAT IN-PLANE L stamping -- 2 barbed THT legs (both pin 1, one node; 5.08mm +/-0.08 pitch, 1.40mm +/-0.05 dia holes, same leg/hole pattern as 63849-1) hang off one end of the strip, and the blade runs ALONG the strip/leg-pitch axis past the blade-side leg, its 6.35mm width spanning 2.54-8.89mm OFF the seating face (8.89 = TE profile height; the blade stands away from the mounting face, it does not lie on it). Reeled (vs 63849-1's loose piece). PLATFORM MOUNTING (owner sketch 2026-07-05, docs/standard-tier-review/blade-fit-check-2026-07-04.md addendum 3): legs horizontal through the vertical daughterboard face, leg pitch vertical, blade pointing STRAIGHT DOWN past the board's bottom edge at the 2.54-8.89mm standoff -- the assembly drops vertically, broadside, into the main-board Keystone 3586 clip's top-entry jaws (the clip's native auto-blade-fuse mode); the daughterboard's own edge floats clear, the tab does the reaching."
				(at 0 0 0)
				(show_name no)
				(do_not_autoplace no)
				(hide yes)
				(effects
					(font
						(size 1.27 1.27)
					)
				)
			)
